<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One column of italic Latin verse, with a page number and running head at the top and a marginal note at the right, beside the last line.</layout>
  <page_number>52</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Ut prisco hospitibus tempore tristium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Nosti, Rhene, tuo flumine connubens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Extorres, veteris matris originem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Et Francis repetunt dum laribus locum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Norunt Helvetiae frigida Martiae Castella in niueis edita cautibus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Et tu, qua Rhodani, dum rapidus fugit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Obseruas thalamum, Naiadibus cano</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Lemanno pofitum, non noua cernere.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Exutas opibus cum patria pios,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Vidisti lachrymans, &amp; referans fores,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Atque ala tenuis tegmine contegens,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Clauis cur Aquilae stemmate sit tuo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Sic coniuncta doces, numine praefide.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Exultabat Aman Gallicus, obstrepens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Regni culminibus, vulgus &amp; infimum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Mulcebat, Melij dogmata persequens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>(Demens, qui penitus credidit Ahalae</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Sublatum esse genus) Iussa tyrannica</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Urgens, qualia non Persicus extudit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Assueri arbitrio regna regens suo.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Ergo, sanguineus ceu lupus (impigrum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Edendi rabidus quem stimulat furor)</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Complet: non satiat visceribus famem,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Nec multum bibitus diffociat sitim</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Crudelem ore cruor guttura quo lauit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Sed tanto sitiens valdius appetit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Quanto plus biberit trux fera sanguinis:</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="right" at="Ergo, sanguineus ceu" line_from="21" line_to="21">Sic</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>Running head letters are widely spaced; read as GVISIACA. The word "praefide" (last line of the second stanza) is doubtful: the printed form is hard to read. "Naiadibus" and "Lemanno" are read from a worn scan. The word "Melij" and "Ahalae" are proper names as printed.</notes>
</page>
